.TH "HTMLVIDEOELEMENT.ENTERPICTUREINPICTURE_EVENT" "3JS" "October 27, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
HTMLVideoElement.enterpictureinpicture_event \- HTMLVideoElement:
enterpictureinpicture event
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[CR]enterpictureinpicture\f[R] event is fired when the
\f[CR]HTMLVideoElement\f[R] enters picture\-in\-picture mode
successfully.
.PP
This event is not cancelable and does not bubble.
.SH SYNTAX
Use the event name in \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqenterpictureinpicture\(dq, (event) => { })
.EE
.PP
Alternatively, assign to the event handler property of the interface:
.IP
.EX
onenterpictureinpicture = (event) => { }
.EE
.SH EVENT TYPE
A \f[CR]PictureInPictureEvent\f[R].
Inherits from \f[CR]Event\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
These examples add an event listener for the HTMLVideoElement\(cqs
\f[CR]enterpictureinpicture\f[R] event, then post a message when that
event handler has reacted to the event firing.
.PP
Using \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] video = document.querySelector(\(dq#video\(dq);
\f[B]const\f[R] button = document.querySelector(\(dq#button\(dq);

\f[B]function\f[R] onEnterPip() {
  console.log(\(dqPicture\-in\-Picture mode activated!\(dq);
}

video.addEventListener(\(dqenterpictureinpicture\(dq, onEnterPip);

button.onclick = () \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  video.requestPictureInPicture();
};
.EE
.PP
Using the \f[CR]onenterpictureinpicture\f[R] event handler property (but
note that this replaces other event listeners added using
\f[CR]onenterpictureinpicture\f[R], if any):
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] video = document.querySelector(\(dq#video\(dq);
\f[B]const\f[R] button = document.querySelector(\(dq#button\(dq);

\f[B]function\f[R] onEnterPip() {
  console.log(\(dqPicture\-in\-Picture mode activated!\(dq);
}

video.onenterpictureinpicture = onEnterPip;

button.onclick = () \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  video.requestPictureInPicture();
};
.EE
